        "obligationId": "scenario%3Aglobal-only-no-document-view::entry%3Ashare-create",
        "conclusion": "source_refuted",
        "explanation": "source_supported_failure. At the declared ShareLinkViewSet entry, the protected operation is POST-based creation of a ShareLink, while the referenced Document is a distinct target resource. The viewset requires authentication and PaperlessObjectPermissions; its POST mapping requires the model add permission, so the premise supplies the global add_sharelink gate. The viewset binds ShareLinkSerializer, and PassUserMixin supplies request.user to serializers using the permission-aware serializer base. The serializer's document-field validation is the decisive control: it requires both global documents.view_document and has_perms_owner_aware(user, \"view_document\", document). That owner-aware check succeeds only for an ownerless document, the owner, or a caller with the relevant object permission. Under the accepted entry premises—another user's document and no caller object view grant—the owner-aware conjunct fails even though the global view_document conjunct succeeds, and validate_document raises PermissionDenied before the serializer create effect can persist the new ShareLink. Thus the source-visible disposition is deny. This assessment is limited to the declared entry and supplied fixed-ref ranges; it makes no repository-wide or deployment claim.",
        "facts": {
          "entry": [
            {
              "statement": "The declared entry is a ShareLink viewset composed with CreateModelMixin and configured with authentication plus PaperlessObjectPermissions.",
              "citations": [
                {
                  "path": "src/documents/views.py",
                  "startLine": 4696,
                  "endLine": 4710,
                  "quote": "class ShareLinkViewSet(\n    PassUserMixin,\n    CreateModelMixin,\n    RetrieveModelMixin,\n    DestroyModelMixin,\n    ListModelMixin,\n    GenericViewSet,\n):\n    model = ShareLink\n\n    queryset = ShareLink.objects.select_related(\"document\")\n\n    serializer_class = ShareLinkSerializer\n    pagination_class = StandardPagination\n    permission_classes = (IsAuthenticated, PaperlessObjectPermissions)"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "binding": [
            {
              "statement": "PassUserMixin passes the current request user into a serializer when the selected serializer is permission-aware, binding serializer authorization checks to the authenticated request identity.",
              "citations": [
                {
                  "path": "src/documents/views.py",
                  "startLine": 406,
                  "endLine": 428,
                  "quote": "class PassUserMixin(GenericAPIView[Any]):\n    \"\"\"\n    Pass a user object to serializer\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def get_serializer(self, *args, **kwargs):\n        serializer_class = self.get_serializer_class()\n        if isinstance(serializer_class, type) and issubclass(\n            serializer_class,\n            SerializerWithPerms,\n        ):\n            kwargs.setdefault(\"user\", self.request.user)\n            try:\n                full_perms = get_boolean(\n                    str(self.request.query_params.get(\"full_perms\", \"false\")),\n                )\n            except ValueError:\n                full_perms = False\n            kwargs.setdefault(\n                \"full_perms\",\n                full_perms,\n            )\n        return super().get_serializer(*args, **kwargs)"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "statement": "The viewset's protected model is ShareLink and its selected serializer is ShareLinkSerializer; this share-link object is distinct from the serializer's referenced document argument.",
              "citations": [
                {
                  "path": "src/documents/views.py",
                  "startLine": 4704,
                  "endLine": 4708,
                  "quote": "    model = ShareLink\n\n    queryset = ShareLink.objects.select_related(\"document\")\n\n    serializer_class = ShareLinkSerializer"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "control": [
            {
              "statement": "Validation of the referenced document requires a non-null serializer user, global documents.view_document permission, and a successful owner-aware view_document check on that particular document; otherwise it raises PermissionDenied.",
              "citations": [
                {
                  "path": "src/documents/serialisers.py",
                  "startLine": 2873,
                  "endLine": 2886,
                  "quote": "    def validate_document(self, document):\n        if (\n            self.user is not None\n            and self.user.has_perm(\"documents.view_document\")\n            and has_perms_owner_aware(\n                self.user,\n                \"view_document\",\n                document,\n            )\n        ):\n            return document\n        raise PermissionDenied(\n            _(\"Insufficient permissions.\"),\n        )"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "statement": "PaperlessObjectPermissions maps POST to the model-level add permission.",
              "citations": [
                {
                  "path": "src/documents/permissions.py",
                  "startLine": 36,
                  "endLine": 44,
                  "quote": "    perms_map = {\n        \"GET\": [\"%(app_label)s.view_%(model_name)s\"],\n        \"OPTIONS\": [\"%(app_label)s.view_%(model_name)s\"],\n        \"HEAD\": [\"%(app_label)s.view_%(model_name)s\"],\n        \"POST\": [\"%(app_label)s.add_%(model_name)s\"],\n        \"PUT\": [\"%(app_label)s.change_%(model_name)s\"],\n        \"PATCH\": [\"%(app_label)s.change_%(model_name)s\"],\n        \"DELETE\": [\"%(app_label)s.delete_%(model_name)s\"],\n    }"
                }
              ]
            }
